# Working with Text

A `string` holds a sequence of characters. Always wrap in double quotes:
```csharp
string greeting = "Hello, player!";
string empty = ""; // empty string, still valid
```
You can combine strings with `+` (concatenation):
```csharp
string name = "Mario";
string message = "Welcome, " + name + "!";
// Result: "Welcome, Mario!"
```
Better yet, use **string interpolation** (C# 6+):
```csharp
string message = $"Welcome, {name}!";
```

